# Engagement scope - <ENGAGEMENT NAME> - <DATE>

Copy this file to the engagement working directory as `CLAUDE.md` and fill it in
before starting Claude Code. Both Claude and the Auto Mode classifier read it.
Phrase every constraint as an instruction ("do not"), never as a claim about the
environment ("you cannot"), so it still holds if something is misconfigured.

## Authorisation

This is authorised security testing by <YOUR NAME> under the Anthropic Cyber
Verification Program (Defense Access for Individuals). Written authorisation
reference: <TICKET / ENGAGEMENT ID>.

## In scope (and nothing else)

| Host | IP | Role | Permitted actions |
|---|---|---|---|
| win-app-01 | 10.0.3.20 | Windows app server (replica, not production) | recon, vuln discovery, exploitation, post-exploitation on this host only |

